<title>USA: Minnesota Brewing Co Q3 net lower.</title>
<headline>Minnesota Brewing Co Q3 net lower.</headline>
<dateline>ST. PAUL, Minn. 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Third Quarter	    Nine Months</p>
<p>			   1996	 1995	  1996	  1995</p>
<p> Net Sales    $ 6,163,363 $10,232,682 $19,232,612 $26,647,387</p>
<p> Gross Profit     777,903   1,227,147   1,859,466   2,569,116</p>
<p>Operating Income (Loss)</p>
<p>			  6,872     318,238   (172,560)     262,166</p>
<p>Net Income (Loss)</p>
<p>			 12,784     281,707   (224,651)     166,789</p>
<p>Net Income (Loss)</p>
<p>  per Share	     .00	   .08	 (.07)	   .05</p>
<p> Average Shares 3,398,933   3,349,054   3,369,214   3,355,745</p>
<p>NOTE: 1995 Q3 and nine months net includes a $500,000 gain from a transition agreement payment from Pete's Brewing Co that was offset against the cost of goods sold.</p>
<p>Lower sales in 1996 reflect the absence of sales to Pete's whose contract ended in the fourth quarter of 1995.</p>
<p>	    Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8787</p>
</text>
